cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Super Spectral — its firmware, DSP design notes, validation
  plan, golden-file manifests or datasets — please cite it as below. Once a
  release exists, prefer the versioned DOI that will be listed here.
type: software
title: "Super Spectral"
abstract: >-
  A wrist-worn singing-voice spectral analyzer on the LilyGO T-Watch S3
  (ESP32-S3) with a single PDM MEMS microphone: the live-capture and
  real-time-display front end of a preset-driven analyzer, with all
  real-time DSP on-device and a Linux companion for offline analysis of
  recorded takes. The repository is built documentation-first: research
  question, prioritized bibliography and acquisition ledger, architecture
  decision records, two-path validation plan (digital injection vs
  acoustic), and a pinned, reproducible ESP-IDF v6.0.2 environment.
authors:
  - family-names: Gomez
    given-names: Alexander
    # ORCID: TBD
keywords:
  - singing voice
  - spectral analysis
  - spectrogram
  - pitch estimation
  - singer's formant
  - ESP32-S3
  - ESP-IDF
  - PDM microphone
  - wearable
  - reproducible research
